Work around GCC 8's LTO dropping layout.cpp's -ffp-contract=off.

Upstream compiles src/frontend/video/layout.cpp with -ffp-contract=off so that
screen placement, which is float arithmetic truncated to pixels, lands on the
same pixel on every architecture; tests/layout_test.cpp pins the result with a
hash over a sweep of layouts. With the project's LTO on, GCC 8 does not keep
that option once layout's functions are inlined into callers compiled without
it, and the dominant_v layout moves its second screen down a pixel in 13 of
3942 sweep cases. Verified by bisection in the LoveRetro toolchain images,
holding -mcpu constant at cortex-a53 so the compiler is the only variable:

  GCC 8.3.0   layout.cpp off, rest LTO-linked without it   layout FAIL
  GCC 8.3.0   same, with -ffp-contract=off on the link too  layout FAIL
  GCC 8.3.0   layout.cpp -fno-lto, rest LTO                 layout pass
  GCC 8.3.0   everything -ffp-contract=off, -O0 to -O3+LTO  layout pass
  GCC 10.3.0  layout.cpp off, rest LTO-linked without it   layout pass

Only GCC 8 builds the file outside LTO; GCC 9 and later keep it in. Placement
runs only when the layout or the output size changes, never per frame, so
nothing is lost by not inlining it. tg5040 and h700 build with GCC 8.3.0,
tg5050 with GCC 10.3.0, so this affects two of the three platforms, and the
shipping dsperate there as well as the test.

Upstream: https://github.com/beebono/DSperate/issues/23

diff --git a/src/frontend/video/CMakeLists.txt b/src/frontend/video/CMakeLists.txt
index a568f26..9817934 100644
--- a/src/frontend/video/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/frontend/video/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -8,3 +8,9 @@ target_include_directories(dsperate_frontend_video PUBLIC ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE
 # Placement is float arithmetic: no fused multiply-add, so every architecture
 # lands on the same pixel (test_layout pins it).
 set_source_files_properties(layout.cpp PROPERTIES COMPILE_OPTIONS "-ffp-contract=off")
+# GCC 8's LTO drops that per-file -ffp-contract=off once layout's code is
+# inlined into callers built without it, so the pixels move anyway. Keep the
+# file out of LTO there; GCC 9 and later honour the option across LTO.
+if(CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_ID STREQUAL "GNU" AND CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_VERSION VERSION_LESS 9)
+  set_property(SOURCE layout.cpp APPEND PROPERTY COMPILE_OPTIONS "-fno-lto")
+endif()
